.TH RAYTRACER 1 "2026-05-17" "raytracer 1.0" "Raytracer Manual"
.SH NAME
raytracer \- physically-based ray tracing renderer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raytracer
.I SCENE_FILE
.RB [ \-\-no\-bvh ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-viewport ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B raytracer
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raytracer
renders a 3D scene to a 2D image using ray tracing. It loads a scene
description from
.IR SCENE_FILE ,
traces primary and secondary rays through the scene, and shades each
pixel with a physically-based integrator.
.PP
By default the renderer opens a live SFML viewport that displays the
image as it is computed. With
.B \-\-no\-viewport
the renderer runs headless and writes the rendered image in PPM format
to a file
.RB ( out.ppm
in the current directory by default; the destination can be overridden
by the JSON configuration passed to
.BR \-\-config ).
.PP
Scene files are accepted in libconfig
.RB ( .cfg )
and glTF
.RB ( .gltf )
formats. The runtime log verbosity is controlled by the
.B RT_LOG_LEVEL
environment variable
.RB ( trace ,
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn ,
.BR error ,
.BR silent ;
default
.BR info ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I SCENE_FILE
Path to the scene description to render. Required for any rendering
invocation. Supported formats are libconfig
.RB ( .cfg )
and glTF
.RB ( .gltf ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-bvh
Disable the BVH (bounding volume hierarchy) acceleration structure.
Intersection tests fall back to a linear scan of every primitive. Useful
for debugging or for very small scenes; significantly slower otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-viewport
Render headless: skip the live SFML display window and write the
rendered image to a PPM file
.RB ( out.ppm
by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Load a JSON render-configuration file describing render settings
(resolution, sample count, output file, etc.). The
.B outputFile
field, when present, overrides the default
.B out.ppm
destination. Only available in builds compiled with
.BR BUILD_BONUS .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit. Must be the only argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Render a scene in the live viewport:
.B raytracer
.I scenes/example.cfg
.TP
Render headless; the image is written to out.ppm:
.B raytracer
.I scenes/example.cfg
.B \-\-no\-viewport
.TP
Render without the BVH acceleration structure:
.B raytracer
.I scenes/example.cfg
.B \-\-no\-bvh
.TP
Render with a custom JSON render configuration (bonus build):
.B raytracer
.I scenes/example.cfg
.B \-\-config
.I config.json
.TP
Increase log verbosity for a single run:
.B RT_LOG_LEVEL=debug
.B raytracer
.I scenes/example.cfg
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scene was rendered successfully.
.TP
.B 84
An error occurred: invalid command-line arguments, an unreadable or
malformed scene file, or an unhandled runtime exception. A diagnostic
message is written to standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppm (5)
.PP
Project documentation and example scenes are available in the
.B README.md
file and the
.B scenes/
directory of the source distribution.
